(C) Prop 7.3(ii) with D* = infinity: walk with increments log(q2(y)/q1(y)), q1 = Bern(1/4), q2 = coin
  increments: y=1 -> 1.0000, y=0 -> -0.5850; mean = 0.2075 = (1/2) log2(4/3) = 0.2075
  lambda = 1.0: last n <= 200000 at which pi1 is the MAP, 20 runs: max 71, median 27
  (with mu(x) ~ x^-3 on x >= 1 and c(x) = 2^{-x^2}: E_mu log2(1/c) = sum x^2 x^-3 / zeta(3) = infinity,
   so D(pi1) = D(pi2) = infinity = D*, both are in P, the log-ratio is bounded, and yet no oscillation.)
